    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24417" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter-prĭmo</span></b> , pressi, pressum,
		3, v. a.
		premo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to press</i> or <i>squeeze to pieces</i>, <i>to crush</i> (ante- and post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui sacerdoti scelestus faucis interpresserit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 3, 2, 41</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to suppress</i>, <i>conceal</i>, <i><span class="en">Min. Fel. Oct.
